  "title": "The Lost-and-Found Silhouette",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "positive public good",
  "premise": "A community host wants to reunite a visitor with a missing mitten, but the lost-and-found box is a jumble. They hang simple item silhouettes above open compartments; the visitor finds the mitten in the matching shape area and leaves a little drawing showing where the box is for the next person.",
  "hook": "The mitten is lost inside lost-and-found.",
  "visible_action": "Objects spill from box; silhouettes appear; compartments sort by item type; mitten pair reunites; location drawing goes on a nearby board.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Organization helps only if people can find the organized place.",
  "gate": "No real names, contact details, or identity documents in the display; public lost-property processes may require verification.",
